{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And they listened.</b> And they accepted from him. And every 'listening' that is acceptance of words — such as this one, and such as ״וַיִּשְׁמַע יַעֲקֹב אֶל אָבִיו״, ״נַעֲשֶׂה וְנִשְׁמָע״ — is translated נְקַבֵּל. And every one that is hearing of the ear — such as ״וַיִּשְׁמְעוּ אֶת קוֹל יְהוָה אֱלֹהִים מִתְהַלֵּךְ בַּגָּן״, ״וְרִבְקָה שֹׁמַעַת״, ״וַיִּשְׁמַע יִשְׂרָאֵל״, ״שָׁמַעְתִּי אֶת תְּלֻנּוֹת״ — all of them are translated וּשְׁמָעוּ, וּשְׁמַעַת, וּשְׁמַע — 'I heard,' in the Targum."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:32.794466625Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}